.* NETCFG: the task menu for network configuration.
:PNLGRP.
:COPYR.(C) COPYRIGHT QUARTZ SYSTEMS 2026.
:CLASS NAME=OPTCL BASETYPE='CHAR 2'.
:ECLASS.
:CLASS NAME=NAMECL BASETYPE='CHAR 10'.
:ECLASS.
:VAR NAME=OPTION CLASS=OPTCL.
:VAR NAME=PANELID CLASS=NAMECL VALUE='NETCFG'.
:KEYL NAME=MENUKEYS HELP='KEYS/MENUKEYS'.
:KEYI KEY=ENTER ACTION=ENTER.
:KEYI KEY=HELP ACTION=HELP.
:KEYI KEY=F1 ACTION=HELP.
:KEYI KEY=F3 ACTION=EXIT.F3=Exit
:KEYI KEY=F4 ACTION='RETURN 4'.F4=Prompt
:KEYI KEY=F9 ACTION=RETRIEVE.F9=Retrieve
:KEYI KEY=F12 ACTION=CANCEL.F12=Cancel
:KEYI KEY=F13 ACTION='MENU INFO'.F13=Information Assistant
:KEYI KEY=F16 ACTION='MENU MAIN'.F16=System Main menu
:EKEYL.
:PANEL NAME=NETCFG HELP=HLPNETCFG KEYL=MENUKEYS ENTER='RETURN 1' TOPSEP=SYSNAM PANELID=PANELID.Network Configuration
:MENU DEPTH='*' SCROLL=YES OPTIONS=OPTION.Select one of the following:
:MENUI OPTION=1 ACTION='CMD ?WRKDIRE' HELP='NETCFG/OPT1'.Work with directory entries
:MENUI OPTION=2 ACTION='CMD ?CFGDSTSRV' HELP='NETCFG/OPT2'.Configure distribution services
:MENUI OPTION=3 ACTION='CMD ?WRKNETJOBE' HELP='NETCFG/OPT3'.Work with network job entries
:MENUI OPTION=4 ACTION='CMD ?CFGRPDS' HELP='NETCFG/OPT4'.Configure VM/MVS bridge
:MENUI OPTION=5 ACTION='CMD ?WRKDOCLIB' HELP='NETCFG/OPT5'.Work with remote document libraries
:MENUI OPTION=7 ACTION='MENU NWSADM' HELP='NETCFG/OPT7'.Network Server administration
:MENUI OPTION=10 ACTION='MENU CFGCMN' HELP='NETCFG/OPT10'.Configure communications and remote hardware
:MENUI OPTION=70 ACTION='MENU CMDNET' HELP='NETCFG/OPT70'.Related commands
:EMENU.
:CMDLINE SIZE=LONG.Selection or command
:EPANEL.
:HELP NAME=HLPNETCFG.Network Configuration - Help
:P.The configuration of the network functions. Most of them belong to SNA
distribution, which this release does not have; option 10 leads to the
lines, devices and TCP/IP.
:P.Type an option number or a command and press Enter. F4 prompts the
command, F9 brings the previous one back, F12 returns to the menu shown
before this one.
:EHELP.
.* Item, key and option help.
:HELP NAME='KEYS/MENUKEYS'.Function keys
:PARML.
:PT.F3=Exit
:PD.Ends the display and returns to where it was started from.
:PT.F4=Prompt
:PD.Prompts the command on the command line, or the command of the
option typed.
:PT.F9=Retrieve
:PD.Puts the last command run back on the command line; press it again
for the one before.
:PT.F12=Cancel
:PD.Returns to the previous display without acting on what was typed.
:PT.F13=Information Assistant
:PD.Shows menu INFO.
:PT.F16=System Main menu
:PD.Shows menu MAIN.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='NETCFG/OPT1'.Work with directory entries
:P.Option 1. Runs the WRKDIRE command&colon. Work with directory
entries.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='NETCFG/OPT2'.Configure distribution services
:P.Option 2. Runs the CFGDSTSRV command&colon. Configure distribution
services.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='NETCFG/OPT3'.Work with network job entries
:P.Option 3. Runs the WRKNETJOBE command&colon. Work with network job
entries.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='NETCFG/OPT4'.Configure VM/MVS bridge
:P.Option 4. Runs the CFGRPDS command&colon. Configure VM/MVS bridge.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='NETCFG/OPT5'.Work with remote document libraries
:P.Option 5. Runs the WRKDOCLIB command&colon. Work with remote document
libraries.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='NETCFG/OPT7'.Network Server administration
:P.Option 7. Shows menu NWSADM&colon. Network Server administration.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='NETCFG/OPT10'.Configure communications and remote hardware
:P.Option 10. Shows menu CFGCMN&colon. Configure communications and
remote hardware.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='NETCFG/OPT70'.Related commands
:P.Option 70. Shows menu CMDNET&colon. Related commands.
:EHELP.
:EPNLGRP.
